{
  "name": "Project Packager",
  "description": "Adds a one-click **Zip Project** button to the project tree toolbar that packages the whole project into a timestamped `.zip` archive and writes it straight into a folder you configure once.\n\n## Features\n- **One-click packaging** – click the archive-icon button in the project tree toolbar to zip the entire currently open project\n- **Configurable target folder** – choose the destination folder once in the project's settings; every subsequent zip is written there automatically, no dialog required\n- **Timestamped archives** – each archive is named `<project-name>_<yyyy-MM-dd_HHmmss>.zip`, so repeated packaging never overwrites a previous archive\n- **Localized settings page** – the *Project Packager* settings page is available in English and German\n\n## How to configure\n1. Open the project's settings (gear icon / *Project Settings*)\n2. Select the *Project Packager* page in the settings navigation\n3. Click *Browse…* and pick the folder that packaged zip archives should be written to\n4. The folder is saved immediately – no separate *Apply* step is needed\n\n## How it works\n1. With a target folder configured, click the zip/compress icon in the project tree toolbar (next to *New*, *Reload*, *Expand All*, *Collapse All*)\n2. The whole project folder is zipped and the archive is written to the configured target folder\n3. A confirmation dialog shows the path of the archive that was written\n\n> **Note:** If no target folder has been configured yet, clicking the toolbar button opens an alert asking you to configure one on the *Project Packager* settings page first.",
  "pluginVersion": "1.0.0",
  "a12Version": "2606",
